From 61555ea3a2b663554271d8bb39bf125b9d8af86d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Yu <josephyu@yahooinc.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:07:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Do not add a map marker before the map panel exists

Decoded from the panic on the device, which had been rebooting roughly once a
minute:

    0x4201e3e3 lv_obj_class_create_obj
    0x420436ff lv_image_create
    0x4207b421 TFTView_320x240::addOrUpdateMap
    0x4207ebdd TFTView_320x240::updatePosition
    0x4213b465 ViewController::packetReceived
    0x42088582 ViewController::receive

lv_image_create(objects.raw_map_panel) with a null parent. The map screen is
built lazily, so both map and objects.raw_map_panel stay null until it has been
opened once - while position packets arrive from the mesh regardless. LVGL
dereferences a parent without checking it, hence StoreProhibited.

The function already tests "if (map)" twice below, so the possibility was known;
those tests simply run after the object creation that crashes. Guarding at the
top instead, on both the map and its panel.

Markers for nodes heard before the map is first opened are skipped rather than
created, and reappear when that node next broadcasts a position. That is the
trade this makes, and it is a better one than panicking every minute.

Supersedes the guard I added in the previous commit: that one protected the node
panel lookup in updatePosition, which is a real instance of the same
operator[]-then-dereference shape but is not what was firing. The backtrace here
was decoded rather than inferred.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
